# LF everywhere, on every platform.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. This host has `core.autocrlf=true` and no .gitattributes,
# so git rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. `tools/doc-check.mjs` matches fenced
# blocks as ```ts\n — LF-anchored — so a CRLF working copy makes EVERY TypeScript
# block in the spec invisible to the gate. When that happened on 2026-08-08 it
# did not fail loudly: the forward field-coverage check iterated an empty set and
# PASSED SILENTLY, while the reverse check produced 33 findings pointing at
# innocent sections. The gate can be made to report "clean" over a parse that
# read nothing, which is the failure the tool was rebuilt in round 7 to end.
#
# `[HARVEST]` in doc-check.mjs is the detector for that class. This file is the
# prevention. Keep both.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
